---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout 
  title="Configuration & CLI Reference" 
  description="Complete configuration options for /etc/duckjump/duckjump.env and duckjump CLI administration commands."
  currentSlug="cli-configuration"
>
  <div class="space-y-8">
    
    <div>
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-800 text-slate-300 border border-slate-700 text-xs font-mono mb-3">
        System Reference
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight">
        Configuration & CLI Reference
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-lg mt-2 leading-relaxed">
        Environment variables reference and CLI administration commands for managing duckJump in headless and automated environments.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Configuration File -->
    <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-800">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">1. Configuration: duckjump.env</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Service settings are stored in <code class="text-amber-300">/etc/duckjump/duckjump.env</code>:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-slate-800 rounded-xl">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs text-slate-300">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900 text-slate-400 font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-[11px] border-b border-slate-800">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3">Variable</th>
              <th class="p-3">Default</th>
              <th class="p-3">Description</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800 font-mono">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-amber-400 font-bold">DUCKJUMP_ADDR</td>
              <td class="p-3">:8443</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-sans text-slate-300">Listen address and port for the HTTPS/WSS web gateway.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-amber-400 font-bold">DUCKJUMP_DB</td>
              <td class="p-3">/var/lib/duckjump/duckjump.db</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-sans text-slate-300">SQLite database file or PostgreSQL connection URL.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-amber-400 font-bold">DUCKJUMP_TLS_CERT</td>
              <td class="p-3">/etc/duckjump/tls.crt</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-sans text-slate-300">Path to the gateway's TLS certificate file.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-amber-400 font-bold">DUCKJUMP_TLS_KEY</td>
              <td class="p-3">/etc/duckjump/tls.key</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-sans text-slate-300">Path to the gateway's TLS private key file (0600).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-amber-400 font-bold">DUCKJUMP_MASTER_KEY_FILE</td>
              <td class="p-3">/etc/duckjump/master.key</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-sans text-slate-300">AES-256 vault encryption key file. Keep backed up!</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-amber-400 font-bold">DUCKJUMP_TRUSTED_PROXIES</td>
              <td class="p-3">127.0.0.1,::1</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-sans text-slate-300">Reverse proxy CIDRs for client IP audit & X-Forwarded headers.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CLI Commands -->
    <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-800">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">2. CLI Administration Commands</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        On Linux package installs, use the <code class="text-amber-300">sudo duckjump</code> wrapper (or <code class="text-amber-300">duckjump-gw</code> directly):
      </p>

      <div class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs text-slate-200 space-y-3">
        <div>
          <span class="text-slate-500"># User and role administration:</span>
          <div class="text-amber-400">sudo duckjump user add alice --role admin --email alice@corp.com</div>
          <div class="text-slate-300">sudo duckjump user passwd alice</div>
          <div class="text-slate-300">sudo duckjump user disable bob</div>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-2 border-t border-slate-800/80">
          <span class="text-slate-500"># Storing encrypted credentials into the vault:</span>
          <div class="text-amber-400">sudo duckjump secret add --name "prod-key" --type ssh-key --file ~/.ssh/id_ed25519</div>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-2 border-t border-slate-800/80">
          <span class="text-slate-500"># Issue a Just-In-Time access grant:</span>
          <div class="text-amber-400">sudo duckjump grant add --user alice --conn "db-server-01" --ttl 2h --upload --download</div>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-2 border-t border-slate-800/80">
          <span class="text-slate-500"># Emergency terminate a live session:</span>
          <div class="text-rose-400">sudo duckjump kill s-8472f10b</div>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-2 border-t border-slate-800/80">
          <span class="text-slate-500"># Zero-downtime migration to PostgreSQL:</span>
          <div class="text-sky-400">sudo duckjump migrate-to-postgres -to 'postgres://duckjump:pwd@pg.internal:5432/duckjump'</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</DocsLayout>
